+# Machine-checked audit — S5-CLM-00003495
+
+## Exact statement replay
+
+`Statement.lean` reconstructs `lt₂`, `IsIncreasing₂`, `maximalLength`, the
+parameterized source proposition, the canonical target abbreviation, and both
+identity transports.  `Audit.lean` elaborates direct forward and reverse type
+probes, so a drift in the implicit binders, hypotheses, real power, eventual
+filter, inequality, or extremal function fails compilation.
+
+## Quantifier audit
+
+`Proof.lean` proves:
+
+```text
+Target hn h → ArbitrarilyLargeConclusion e
+```
+
+and independently proves that an unbounded-witness predicate need not be
+eventually true.  These declarations compile at trust level zero.  Their
+axiom census is exactly:
+
+```text
+[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]
+```
+
+## Root status
+
+There is no target root.  The provider body's census includes `sorryAx`, so it
+is excluded.  The human product anchor closes an unbounded subsequence, not
+the stronger eventual-all conclusion frozen in the formal row.  The remaining
+machine cut set therefore contains one exact node: proof of `Target hn h` for
+arbitrary frozen parameters and hypotheses.
+
+Static scanning finds no executable placeholder, claim-specific axiom,
+unsafe declaration, bodyless oracle, or provider proof import.  The clean
+compilation and audit are valid diagnostics but intentionally do not set
+`machine_complete`.  The local diagnostic module is recorded as an
+`M0-L-candidate` frontier; this label is not an exact-root claim.
